# Real-Time Digital Twin Architecture for Additive Manufacturing

This repository contains the implementation, analysis code, processed data, results, and supporting materials associated with the study:

**“A Real-Time Digital Twin Architecture for Additive Manufacturing: IoT Telemetry Acquisition, Cyber-Physical Synchronization, and a Proof-of-Concept Predictive Analytics Pipeline.”**

The project demonstrates an integrated real-time Digital Twin (DT) workflow for a **Prusa i3 MK3S fused deposition modeling (FDM) 3D printer**. The implemented architecture connects physical machine telemetry with IoT communication, data processing, cyber-physical synchronization, time-series storage, predictive analytics, and monitoring within a unified experimental framework.

---

## Project Overview

The main objective of this work is to demonstrate how a real manufacturing asset can be connected to a Digital Twin infrastructure that supports:

- real-time telemetry acquisition;
- IoT-based communication;
- cyber-physical synchronization;
- data preprocessing and feature engineering;
- time-series data storage;
- machine-learning-based predictive analytics;
- analytical output storage;
- monitoring and visualization.

The implementation is based on the first three operational layers of a broader **Causal Digital Twin Framework (CDTF)**.

### Implemented layers

1. **Data Acquisition and Integration**
2. **Cyber-Physical Synchronization**
3. **AI-Driven Analytics and Monitoring**

The fourth layer, **Causal Inference and Modeling**, is outside the scope of the present implementation and is reserved for future development.

---

## Experimental Platform

The experimental system is based on a:

**Prusa i3 MK3S FDM 3D Printer**

Operational information was collected from the printer together with external measurements and processed through the Digital Twin infrastructure.

The implementation uses technologies including:

- Python
- MQTT
- Node-RED
- OctoPrint
- PostgreSQL
- TimescaleDB
- pgAdmin
- Grafana
- Docker

---

## Digital Twin Workflow

The implemented workflow can be summarized as:

```text
Physical 3D Printer
        |
        v
Sensors / OctoPrint / External Measurements
        |
        v
MQTT Communication
        |
        v
Node-RED / Python Data Processing
        |
        v
Cyber-Physical Synchronization
        |
        v
PostgreSQL / TimescaleDB
        |
        v
Data Preprocessing
        |
        v
Feature Engineering
        |
        v
Predictive Analytics
        |
        v
Analytical Output Storage
        |
        v
Monitoring / Visualization
